    ('h', '2.7', 'Summarized Outcome of the Literature Review'),
    ('p', 'The literature establishes that matching the network to the entanglement structure is the key design decision, that MPS/TT simulation of circuits is controlled by truncated Schmidt coefficients, that PEPS ground states can be obtained by imaginary-time evolution with local truncation, and that MERA energies can be optimized with environment-based updates. It does not provide a single like-for-like measurement of the three on common footing, which is the gap this project addresses.'),
