    ('p', '*Truncation and PEPS-aware optimization.* The optimized angles are applied gate by gate to a PEPS with truncation to D. Because the truncation has no cheap exact gradient, the truncated-PEPS energy itself is then minimized with Adam [11] using central finite-difference gradients evaluated in parallel on 10 processes, a cosine-decayed step from 0.03 to 0.003, and a warm start from the exact-circuit angles. 200 steps were used for 3×3 and 60 for 4×4.'),
    ('f', 'f32_pepsflow.png', 'Fig. 3.2', 'Pipeline of the PEPS variational study', 5.9),
    ('h', '3.5', 'Study 3: MERA for the Critical Ising Chain'),
    ('p', 'The model is H = −Σ Z_{i}Z_{i+1} − Σ X_{i} with periodic boundaries and L = 2^{n} sites. The exact energy was computed from the free-fermion formula and checked against sparse exact diagonalization for L ≤ 12. The finite binary MERA places isometries on sites (2j, 2j+1) and disentanglers on (2j+1, 2j+2), caps the site dimension at χ, and coarse-grains from L sites to two. The energy is obtained by ascending every Hamiltonian term through the layers (contractions found once with opt_einsum and cached) and diagonalizing the two-site top Hamiltonian.'),
    ('p', 'Tensors are optimized with Evenbly–Vidal updates [13]: the environment of each tensor is obtained by back-propagating through the same coarse-graining network, and the tensor is replaced by −AB^{T}, where Γ = ASB^{T} is the SVD of its environment. A step is accepted only if it lowers the energy. One layer is updated per iteration, cycling through the layers. Runs used L = 16 and χ = 2, 4 and 8 for 200, 200 and 120 iterations.'),
