    ('p', 'Several deviations from the expectations in the proposal should be noted. The simple-update error on 2×2 does not decrease monotonically with D. A Néel start for the VQE does not converge, whereas a singlet-dimer start does. The standard L-BFGS optimizer stopped after a few iterations on the truncated-PEPS energy, probably because that landscape is not smooth (the retained subspace can jump when singular values are nearly degenerate, as they are for a dimer start; this explanation was not verified), and Adam was used instead. The MPS/TT memory column reads 0.0 for most runs because it measures a difference in process memory, so memory is not compared. The proposal’s illustrative run-time and memory figures were replaced by measured values, and GPU acceleration was not available on the hardware used.'),
